Held at 6.0.0 rather than 5.5.0 because of the IME fix in 52e8a75e: 5.5.0's
CompositionHelper records the end of the composed text only from the timer
compositionupdate schedules, so a typist fast enough to commit the next
syllable before that timer runs loses the syllable in between. Korean commits
a syllable every two or three keystrokes, so the loss is continuous rather
than occasional. tests/web/composition_check.js pins it.

Local patch (claunch-xa0j7) — re-apply on upgrade; tests/web/termselect_check.js
fails until it is:
  SelectionService.disable(){this.clearSelection(),this._enabled=!1}
  -> disable(){this._enabled&&this.clearSelection(),this._enabled=!1}
Every DECSET 9/1000/1002/1003 runs the activeProtocol setter, which fires
onProtocolChange even when the protocol is unchanged, and the handler calls
disable(). Claude Code re-sends its mouse modes while it redraws (58 times in
one session's output), so a Shift/Option+drag selection -- the only selection
possible while mouse tracking is on -- was cleared mid-drag. Disabling an
already disabled service now keeps it; turning tracking on still clears an
ordinary selection, as upstream does.
